<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore December M1 rises 6.7 pct on year - MAS.</title>
<headline>Singapore December M1 rises 6.7 pct on year - MAS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Money supply figures.</p>
<p>	   (in billions of Singapore dollars)</p>
<p>				 Dec     Nov     Dec 95</p>
<p>M-1 (narrow money)	 27.04   26.51    25.35</p>
<p>M-2			   111.95  110.92   101.97</p>
<p>M-3 (broad money)	 139.84  137.91   128.84</p>
<p>Demand deposits	    16.75   16.53    15.44</p>
<p>Currency in active	 10.29    9.98     9.91</p>
<p>circulation</p>
<p>Note - The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said narrow money supply (M1) grew by 6.7 percent year-on-year in December, compared with 8.3 percent in November.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
